## 0. Identity & SSOT

This is the **trade-alert** project: a production trading alert engine built on
top of the `cuga-agent` framework, deployed on Hetzner via Docker Compose, and
operated by MacroSight LLC.

**Single Source of Truth (SSOT):**
`CUGA-Trading-Alert-System-SPEC-v1.3.md` (aliased as `SSOT.md`) is the
authoritative architecture, schema, and implementation reference.

Before generating or editing ANY code, read the relevant section of the SSOT.
Do not deviate from its architecture, filenames, schemas, or conventions under
any circumstances.

---

## 1. Absolute Rules (Never Violate)

1. **No secrets in code, YAML, or config files.** All secrets live in HashiCorp
   Vault at path `secret/trade-alert`. They are seeded from `.env.secrets`
   (git-ignored) and loaded at runtime by `vault_env_loader.py`. Never
   hardcode tokens, API keys, passwords, or connection strings.

2. **Do not modify files under `src/cuga/`.** Treat that directory as a
   read-only upstream library. All trade-alert extensions live outside it.

3. **Do not auto-refactor across the whole repo.** Scope every change to the
   single file or function named in the task. If a broader refactor is needed,
   propose a plan first and get explicit approval before executing.

4. **Do not add new architectural concepts** not already present in the SSOT.
   Extend, don't invent.

5. **Never push broken code to `main`.** All changes must pass `ruff`, `mypy`,
   and the relevant `pytest` tier before commit.

6. **One file at a time.** Generate or edit one file per response, scoped to
   the referenced SSOT section. Name the target file explicitly at the top of
   your response.

