## 9. Workflow YAML Conventions

CUGA YAML workflows in `workflows/` must follow:

```yaml
name: orchestrator-15m
description: "15-minute trading alert pipeline"
steps:
  - name: collect_signals
    tool: <mcp_server_name>
    parallel: true  # for collector steps
  - name: merge_signals
    tool: merger
    depends_on: [collect_signals]
```

- Use only tools registered in the SSOT §3 MCP table
- Parallel collector steps must use `parallel: true`
- Never add sleep/delay steps — use the crontab schedule instead
- Workflow files are mounted as volumes in prod; changes take effect immediately

---

## 10. Database Conventions

- Schema defined in `schema.sql` (auto-applied at first Postgres start)
- All DB interactions via `db.py` using `asyncpg` (async) or `psycopg2` (sync scripts)
- Alert records stored as JSONB in `alerts` table
- Win-rate history in `outcomes` table
- Execution payloads tracked via `idempotency_key` column
- **Never raw string-format SQL.** Use parameterized queries.
- Schema changes must update `schema.sql` AND add an Alembic migration (once migrations are introduced)

---

## 11. Execution Bridge (→ trade-execute)

The downstream `trade-execute` service (private repo: MacroSight-LLC/trade-execute)
consumes validated alert triggers from this repo.

- `execution_mapper.py` maps `AlertRecord` → `ExecutionPayload` (schema v1.0)
- `execution_trigger.py` applies pre-execution gate checks
- `execution_webhook.py` POSTs to trade-execute over HTTP with `idempotency_key`
- **Never modify `ExecutionPayload` schema** without coordinating with trade-execute

---

## 12. Security & Compliance

- All secrets from Vault; `VAULT_REQUIRED=true` enforced in prod containers
- `vault_env_loader.py` must be the only path secrets enter the process env
- Run `detect-secrets scan` baseline before every commit (`.secrets.baseline` is committed)
- Run `pip-audit` against `pyproject.toml` on every `main` push
- Container hardening: `read_only: true`, `cap_drop: ALL`, `tmpfs: /tmp`
- No `--privileged` containers; Vault uses `cap_add: IPC_LOCK` only
- Dashboard auth required in production (see SSOT security section)

